<article class="env-lemma" id="0DWS">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DWS">Lemma <span data-tag="0DWS">51.2.3</span>.</a> Let $I, J \subset A$ be finitely generated ideals of a ring $A$. If $M$ is an $I$-power torsion module, then the canonical map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  H^ i_{V(I) \cap V(J)}(M) \to H^ i_{V(J)}(M)  \]
</div>
  <p> is an isomorphism for all $i$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Use the spectral sequence of Dualizing Complexes, Lemma <a href="/tag/0BJC" data-tag="0BJC">47.9.6</a> to reduce to the statement $R\Gamma _ I(M) = M$ which is immediate from the construction of local cohomology in Dualizing Complexes, Section <a href="/tag/0952" data-tag="0952">47.9</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>